{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Computes the prime factors of an integer n, returning them as a sorted list with multiplicity.\"\"\"\n    factors = []\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors\n    d = 3\n    while d * d <= n:\n        while n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            n //= d\n        d += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be a prime factor itself\n    if n > 1:\n        factors.append(n)\n\n    return factors\n```"}
