{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "def sort_even(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function sorts elements at even indices of a list in ascending order\n    while preserving elements at odd indices, returning a new list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    output_list = [None] * n  # Create a new list of the same length as input_list.\n\n    even_indexed_values = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Collect all elements from even indices.\n            even_indexed_values.append(l[i])\n\n    even_indexed_values.sort()  # Sort the collected even-indexed elements.\n\n    even_ptr = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 2 != 0:  # If the current index is odd.\n            output_list[i] = l[i]  # Preserve the original element.\n        else:  # If the current index is even.\n            output_list[i] = even_indexed_values[even_ptr]  # Place the next sorted even element.\n            even_ptr += 1\n\n    return output_list"}
