{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "def decode_cyclic(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the cyclic shift applied to every group of three characters in a string.\n    Groups of fewer than three characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    decoded_parts = []\n    n = len(s)\n    for i in range(0, n, 3):\n        group = s[i:i+3]\n        if len(group) == 3:\n            # Reverses the shift from `xyz` -> `yzx` back to `xyz`.\n            # If group is 'yzx', decoded is `x + y + z` which is `group[2] + group[0] + group[1]`.\n            decoded_parts.append(group[2] + group[0] + group[1])\n        else:\n            decoded_parts.append(group)\n\n    return \"\".join(decoded_parts)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes as input string encoded with encode_cyclic function. Returns decoded string.\n    Reverses the cyclic encoding by shifting the last character to the beginning for groups of three.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Split string into groups of three characters, identical to encode_cyclic.\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n\n    # Decode each group by applying the inverse cyclic shift if length is 3, otherwise leave unchanged.\n    decoded_groups = [(group[-1] + group[:-1]) if len(group) == 3 else group for group in groups]\n\n    # Join the decoded groups to form the final string.\n    return \"\".join(decoded_groups)\n```"}
