{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "```python\ndef prime_fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_perfect_square(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given integer is a perfect square.\"\"\"\n        if num < 0:\n            return False\n        s = int(num**0.5)\n        return s * s == num\n\n    def is_fibonacci(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a number is Fibonacci using the 5x^2 +/- 4 property.\"\"\"\n        val1 = 5 * num * num + 4\n        val2 = 5 * num * num - 4\n        return is_perfect_square(val1) or is_perfect_square(val2)\n\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given integer is a prime number.\"\"\"\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        # Check odd divisors up to the square root of num.\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    count = 0\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    # Iterate to find the n-th number that is both Fibonacci and prime.\n    while True:\n        fib_num = a + b\n        a, b = b, fib_num\n\n        if fib_num > 1:\n            if is_prime(fib_num):\n                # Verify it is a Fibonacci number, as per the design.\n                if is_fibonacci(fib_num):\n                    count += 1\n                    if count == n:\n                        return fib_num\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "```python\ndef triples_sum_to_zero(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there are three distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n    Returns True if such a triplet exists, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n - 1):\n            for k in range(j + 1, n):\n                if l[i] + l[j] + l[k] == 0:\n                    return True\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_divisible_by(number: int, divisor: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is perfectly divisible by a given divisor.\"\"\"\n    return number % divisor == 0\n\ndef _count_digit_occurrences(number: int, digit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts occurrences of a specific digit in an integer.\"\"\"\n    return str(number).count(str(digit))\n\ndef fizz_buzz(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n which are divisible by 11 or 13.\n    >>> fizz_buzz(50)\n    0\n    >>> fizz_buzz(78)\n    2\n    >>> fizz_buzz(79)\n    3\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sevens_count = 0\n    for x in range(1, n):\n        is_divisible_by_11 = _is_divisible_by(x, 11)\n        is_divisible_by_13 = _is_divisible_by(x, 13)\n\n        if is_divisible_by_11 or is_divisible_by_13:\n            total_sevens_count += _count_digit_occurrences(x, 7)\n    return total_sevens_count\n```"}
