{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```python\ndef fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number.\n    >>> fib(10)\n    55\n    >>> fib(1)\n    1\n    >>> fib(8)\n    21\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    # For n=1, the loop range(0) does not run, b remains 1, which is correct for fib(1).\n    # For n=2, range(1) runs once, a becomes 1, b becomes 1. This means the 2nd fib number is 1.\n    # For n=3, range(2) runs twice, a becomes 1, b becomes 2. This means the 3rd fib number is 2.\n    # The loop needs to run n-1 times to get to the nth Fibonacci number starting from F(1)=1.\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n\n```"}
